WEBVTT

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:09.290
"February 13th"

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:10.700
"February 14th"

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:14.200
I've come for my chocolate.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.870
Sorry, what?

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:21.330
I was promised chocolate!

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.410
Oh, you're talking about Valentine's Day.

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:26.620
Yes, that. Exactly.

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:31.250
Where'd you hear that from?
Do we even have any chocolate?

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:33.120
I'd like some chocolate from you, too, Little.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:34.410
What?

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:40.000
Um... Sure, if you give me some, too.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.910
Why, though?

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:45.580
Because that's how Valentine's works.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:47.120
Oh, I see.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:49.080
--I think so! Take that, and that, and that!

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:53.040
--In that case, I shall prepare some
for you the next time we meet!
--I think so! Take that, and that, and that!

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.290
Yipee!

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:57.330
I couldn't sleep.

00:00:57.330 --> 00:01:02.950
This happens every time, so there's
a part of me that just expects it, but...

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:04.620
I'm just stuck.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:10.750
"Does tomorrow work for you?
Can you still hang out?"

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:10.750
"I sure can."

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:13.500
Will this work out?

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:18.620
Maybe Shimamura started hibernating
in her <i>kotatsu </i>and won't come out.

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:27.200
"Kay, thanks!"
"Sure!"

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.790
"Kay, thanks!"
"Sure!"
"Morning!"

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:30.450
"Morning!"

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:34.330
Heya.

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:18.160
Morning.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:22.250
--Just one look at Shimamura warms my heart.
No wonder she's my sun.

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:24.290
--We have an English quiz today, don't we?
--Just one look at Shimamura warms my heart.
No wonder she's my sun.

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:25.160
--Ayup.
--Just one look at Shimamura warms my heart.
No wonder she's my sun.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:26.250
--Yup.
--Just one look at Shimamura warms my heart.
No wonder she's my sun.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:28.580
--You two seem confident.
--Just one look at Shimamura warms my heart.
No wonder she's my sun.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:30.160
My sun...

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:31.750
I figured if I kept calling her that,

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:32.950
--it'd eventually be less embarrassing,
but it's not.

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:35.540
--Let me see your notes later.
--it'd eventually be less embarrassing,
but it's not.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:36.950
Sure.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.870
Wait... Chocolate already?

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:53.580
I brought it, so don't worry.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:04:02.080
Right. I get it, but now I feel like
I'm being told to wait.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:03.700
I feel like I'm...

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:05.830
...basically Shimamura's puppy.

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:10.750
But I mean, if I was a pup,
maybe Shimamura would hold me.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.080
I could curl up on her lap...

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:16.790
And she'd do all kinds of things.

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:20.700
Being Shimamura's pup would be like the best.

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:24.540
Wait, wait, wait.

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:30.500
I've been pretty unfortunate up until now,
but now I know for certain...

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:33.410
I'm actually pretty stupid lately.

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:38.790
So...

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:41.080
We're going to go hang out now, right?

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:45.750
Is there somewhere you wanted to go?

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:49.700
I-I want to go to Nagoya!

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:54.330
Er... Um... Is that a bit too far?

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:55.830
Nagoya?

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:03.040
I see, so that's how this is.

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:04.540
Wait, what?

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:07.040
It's fine. Let's go.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:09.580
I've been wanting to go, too.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.620
So what are we going to do in Nagoya, anyway?

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:14.910
Um...

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:18.790
Buy some chocolate.
Um... I haven't bought any yet.

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:22.870
Oh, I just thought it'd be fresher
if I bought some the day of...

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:28.620
I see, I see. Well, that's great.

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:33.250
What's going on? Maybe Shimamura's
more excited than I thought she'd be.

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:34.330
But...

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:37.410
Every time I see her smile...

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:41.160
Oh, your chocolate.

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:45.790
You don't get to see it until you buy yours.

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:48.870
If I gave you yours now, it wouldn't
be an exchange, would it?

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.620
Yeah...

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:56.290
Maybe I really am just Shimamura's puppy...

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:01.910
Oh, by the way, Adachi...

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:06.250
You don't need to change into
your Chinese dress today?

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:07.290
Chinese dress?

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:10.540
Yeah, like you did on Christmas.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:19.750
If you'd rather have me wear that,
I'll go change...

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:25.080
W-Well, if you want me to...

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:28.870
Er, I mean, we don't want to leave too late...

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:29.870
"Limited Express"      "Toyohashi"
Special Rapid Train"   "Toyohashi"

00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:32.370
Come on! We'll make the train if we run.

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:33.700
Hey--

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.540
Hurry!

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:39.500
Now time for a breather.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:42.410
I'm surprise you knew the transfer time.

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:44.370
Yeah...

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.290
--The train bound for Toyohashi
is now departing from lane four.

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:48.120
--Hurry, Adachi!
--The train bound for Toyohashi
is now departing from lane four.

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:50.910
Please be careful of the closing doors.

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:59.500
We made it... Though just barely.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:00.750
Hm...

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:05.910
Oh, there's an open seat. Just one.

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:12.000
Why don't you take it, Adachi?

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.790
No, you can have it, Shimamura.

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:17.950
No, you should sit, Adachi.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:20.370
You were sleeping during class.

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:23.790
Huh? That's because...

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:26.750
Oh, so you really were asleep.

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:28.040
Huh?

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:32.040
O-Okay, I guess I'll take it.

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:34.580
Say...

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:39.620
Does... my face look weird?

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:40.870
What?

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:46.910
U-Um, Shimamura?

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:48.620
S-Sorry...

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:52.040
So... It's about 20 minutes to Nagoya.

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:54.830
It's pretty boring until then, huh?

00:07:54.830 --> 00:08:00.620
Huh? Yeah... Then why don't we play <i>shiritori</i>?

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:05.370
<i>Shiritori</i>? Nice. In that case... Apple [<i>ringo</i>]!

00:08:05.370 --> 00:08:09.620
Go? Go... <i>Gomoku </i>soba<i>.</i>

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:11.580
Jeez, you are a kid, right?

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:15.290
Ba... Ba... Basketball [<i>basuketobooru</i>].

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:18.160
Ru... Ru... <i>Ruibe</i>.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:22.660
<i>Ruibe</i>? Seriously, Adachi...

00:08:25.450 --> 00:08:29.700
I... I... Ice cream [<i>aisu</i>].

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:33.370
Su... Su... Su...

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:36.580
Five... Four...

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:38.290
Su?!

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:46.450
Love [<i>suki</i>].

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:51.660
--Two... One.
--Su... Su... Sugyaa!

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.830
I'm sorry, what?

00:08:55.830 --> 00:09:00.580
Su... Su... Su... Sugakiya.

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:02.450
Oh, you just said it too fast.

00:09:03.450 --> 00:09:05.830
Thank you, Sugakiya.

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:08.370
Nagoya, Nagoya.

00:09:08.370 --> 00:09:11.250
Please make sure to take all of your...

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:15.330
Wow, there's a huge line.

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:17.250
Maybe we should go there.

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:20.700
But if I line up, I'm just going
to make you wait.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:22.330
Yeah...

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:26.500
Let's see... There's still time.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:30.700
So what should we do next to kill some time?

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:36.200
Huh? Um... M-Maybe thumb wrestle?

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:38.750
Sure, I guess.

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:40.000
Here.

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:42.910
Hup.

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:50.870
Eleven victories and three losses. I win!

00:09:50.870 --> 00:09:54.870
Man, thumb wrestling can get pretty heated.

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:55.950
Yeah.

00:09:57.830 --> 00:10:03.950
Shimamura seems to be all smiles today,
which is throwing me off.

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:05.620
Every time I see her smile,

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:10.500
I have to stop my cheek muscles
from relaxing into a dumb expression.

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:11.870
Huh?

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:14.540
So here's the big reveal.

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:21.910
Here you go. Your Valentine's chocolate.

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:27.750
I actually bought some from here yesterday.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.500
"February 14th"

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:33.750
"February 13th"

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:37.160
Heya.

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:41.000
Good evening. Wait, I guess it's still hello.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:43.950
It doesn't matter.

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:45.120
I see.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:47.580
So, you have something you wanted to shop for?

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:48.910
Yup, chocolate.

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:51.790
Ah... Do you have a boyfriend, Shima?

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:53.120
Nope.

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:56.700
I'm just getting some to give to a friend.

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:58.290
Huh...?

00:10:59.330 --> 00:11:00.620
Yup.

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:03.950
Well, let's go.

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:05.410
S-Sure...

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:10.580
The train bound for Toyohashi
is about to depart from lane four.

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:13.830
Please be careful of the closing doors.

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:21.370
We just made it.

00:11:21.370 --> 00:11:24.000
Yup, just barely.

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:26.080
Looks like there's one seat open.

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:28.000
Oh, yeah.

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:31.620
--Why don't you take it?
--Why don't you sit, Shima?

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:35.450
Then I guess I'll take it.

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:36.660
Sure.

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:50.580
So... You're in high school, right?

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:51.750
Huh?

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:56.750
Do you see my uniform and bag?

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:58.040
Right.

00:11:58.040 --> 00:12:01.080
But I guess you're in high school, too.

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:05.080
Well, yeah. Have you actually
been going to school?

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:09.790
Somewhat. Looks like you need
to redye your hair.

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:13.540
Yeah... I've been trying to decide
what to do with it.

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:15.330
Huh...?

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:19.830
By the way, Shima...

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:23.830
What did you call me when we were little?

00:12:23.830 --> 00:12:25.790
Huh?

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:32.330
Wait, Shima! Shima!

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:46.620
Honestly, I don't remember.

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:48.620
Oh...

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:50.450
I see.

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:55.040
Shima, you've really changed.

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:58.450
Yeah...

00:12:58.450 --> 00:13:00.540
I did.

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:08.410
Change is an understatement.
I was basically a stranger before.

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:11.540
I used to be insanely cheerful, super friendly,

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:13.620
dumb, and free...

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:17.910
I wonder if that's what Tarumi
expects me to be now.

00:13:17.910 --> 00:13:21.700
Hey, remember when there was a murder here?

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:22.750
Huh?

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:24.040
There was?

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:26.250
Yeah, there was.

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:27.750
Isn't the big city scary?

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:29.370
For real.

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:35.750
That's why being with Tarumi
is honestly a bit uncomfortable.

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:37.290
It's slightly different,

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:39.750
but I sorta feel like Adachi right now.

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:45.200
Yeah... Reality doesn't change
as gracefully as memories.

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:51.330
I actually bought some from here yesterday.

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:53.370
Oh, reall--

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:56.160
Huh? What?!

00:13:56.160 --> 00:13:58.830
So anyway, let's exchange chocolates.

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:01.620
Yay, congrats.

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:03.620
Congrats?

00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:07.330
Th-Then, uh... Congrats.

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:10.870
Don't just let them sit in your room.
Make sure you eat them, okay?

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:18.120
Oh, then let's eat them now.

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:20.290
Wait, now? Right here?

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:22.750
Yup. Right now.

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:25.500
Man, you don't waste any time.

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:37.500
Wow, it's good.

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:39.660
Do you really think that?

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:42.700
Huh? Uh... Yeah.

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:44.370
Huh...?

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:59.160
Okay, I guess you're telling the truth.

00:15:03.450 --> 00:15:06.620
Is there a way to make her doubt me again?

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:13.410
D-Do you want one, Shimamura?

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:16.000
Sure, why not?

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:23.790
Here, say, "Ah."

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:26.500
Huh? Um...

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:32.370
Oh, then...

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:42.120
Ah...

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:47.410
Yup, it's good.

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:48.790
Right?

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:54.120
I think it's about time.

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:56.200
For what?

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:58.290
Just follow me.

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:05.950
Okay, there it is.

00:16:05.950 --> 00:16:08.250
It should start around 6 PM...

00:16:08.250 --> 00:16:09.410
What will?

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:10.830
"Special Valentine's Day Promotion"

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:13.370
"Special Valentine's Day Promotion"

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:13.370
It's starting! Let's go, Adachi!

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:15.540
"Special Valentine's Day Promotion"

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:15.540
H-Huh?

00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:18.040
"We'll share your messages"

00:16:18.250 --> 00:16:20.540
Um... What is this?

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:23.790
"I love you, Kazuki!! Forever! -Makiko"

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:30.580
"I love you, Take! -Mizu"

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:37.830
"I hope we can continue to stay close"

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:50.000
Shima?

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:51.750
Oh, sorry.

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:54.160
Should we head home?

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:56.200
Yeah.

00:16:56.200 --> 00:17:01.000
I think we were expecting this
to be a lot more fun.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:04.830
There were probably more things
that should've happened.

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:11.370
But in reality, all that remains
is this bothersome heavy mood.

00:17:11.370 --> 00:17:14.750
This is probably my fault.

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:21.370
"Does tomorrow work for you?
Can you still hang out?"

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:24.700
What is it?

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:26.750
Huh? Oh, nothing.

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:29.500
"Does tomorrow work for you?
Can you still hang out?"

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:29.500
"I sure can."

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:30.250
"I sure can."

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:33.500
Well, I'll see you later.

00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:36.080
Sorry to drag you around today.

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:38.080
Oh, it's fine.

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:41.750
Well... See you.

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:45.750
There's something so lingering.

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:48.830
Something incomplete.

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:52.250
What are you supposed to do at times like this?

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:56.620
What did you call me when we were little?

00:17:56.620 --> 00:18:00.160
Hm... Hrm...

00:18:03.620 --> 00:18:06.120
Taru!

00:18:13.120 --> 00:18:17.410
Dang it! Listen to me, Taru!

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:21.120
See ya!

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:25.750
I can't let go of the present.

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:26.200
--People can't change that easily.

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:29.700
--Taru...
--People can't change that easily.

00:18:29.700 --> 00:18:31.830
See ya!

00:18:31.830 --> 00:18:34.620
Shima!

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:39.370
"I hope we can continue to stay close!"

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:39.370
My past is connected by briars,

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:41.000
"I hope we can continue to stay close!"

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:41.000
so when I try to reflect upon it,
I'm hurt by my incomplete self from the past.

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:44.200
so when I try to reflect upon it,
I'm hurt by my incomplete self from the past.

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:45.500
And yet...

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:45.950
"-Hogetsu Shimamura"

00:18:45.950 --> 00:18:50.000
"-Hogetsu Shimamura"

00:18:45.950 --> 00:18:50.000
There are times I want to reach into the briars.

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:50.620
"I hope we can continue to stay close!
-Hogetsu Shimamura"

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:50.620
There are times I want to reach into the briars.

00:18:50.620 --> 00:18:55.000
"I hope we can continue to stay close!
-Hogetsu Shimamura"

00:18:50.620 --> 00:18:55.000
Even if that means I prick myself and bleed...

00:18:56.790 --> 00:19:02.580
"I hope we can continue to stay close!
-Hogetsu Shimamura"

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:06.410
Shimamura... Wait, is that you?

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:10.700
There's this fortunetelling bit
on this nightly TV program.

00:19:10.700 --> 00:19:13.290
They were asking for entries,
so I tried sending it in.

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:14.540
"Libra"

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:18.290
Today's lucky letter is... D!

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:23.290
I figured I'd never see it,
so I put something mild... Ah.

00:19:23.290 --> 00:19:27.040
"I hope we can continue to stay close!
-Hogetsu Shimamura"

00:19:23.290 --> 00:19:27.040
It's already over? That was fast.

00:19:27.290 --> 00:19:29.120
Um...

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:33.040
Wh-What exactly did you mean by close?

00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:37.660
Huh? What did I mean?

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:40.620
Um... Did you need an actual example?

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:42.540
I was just wondering, like,
what kind of direction you meant...

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:45.580
Like, friendship?

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:48.870
Yay!

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:52.950
Something like that?

00:19:52.950 --> 00:19:56.540
Uh... Yeah, something like that.

00:19:57.790 --> 00:19:59.330
Yay...

00:19:59.330 --> 00:20:02.910
But I think it was perfect to see this with you.

00:20:02.910 --> 00:20:04.450
Huh?

00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:09.620
When I was entering this thing,
your face popped into my head.

00:20:09.620 --> 00:20:12.330
So I tried to reflect that into my message.

00:20:18.830 --> 00:20:22.370
What's... wrong?

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:33.040
Adachi?

00:20:43.330 --> 00:20:45.500
Wh-What the hell?

00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:47.120
S-Sorry...

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:51.450
Uh, you just startled me. Um...

00:20:51.450 --> 00:20:55.410
Yeah, no more surprise glomps, okay?

00:20:55.410 --> 00:20:58.000
O-Okay...

00:20:58.000 --> 00:21:00.750
Huh? I can then?

00:21:00.750 --> 00:21:01.870
Huh?

00:21:01.870 --> 00:21:06.620
So... If I ask you first,
it's okay, to uh, do this?

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:09.540
Huh? You want to hug me?

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:17.250
Uh... why?

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:25.910
Huh? Well... Because it's warm.

00:21:28.290 --> 00:21:30.250
L-Let's warm up!

00:21:35.830 --> 00:21:40.410
Well, whatever! Come get some! Yeah!

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:54.700
Ow...

00:21:57.250 --> 00:22:03.250
W-Well, I guess this is one way to get closer...

00:22:03.250 --> 00:22:09.870
Though you're so skinny, Adachi,
that neither one of us are going to get warm.

00:22:09.870 --> 00:22:13.830
I wonder if everyone around us
thought we were weird.

00:22:13.830 --> 00:22:16.330
Were they laughing at us?

00:22:16.330 --> 00:22:19.540
I could only see Shimamura.

00:22:19.540 --> 00:22:23.040
Any place I could do that made it the best.

00:22:23.040 --> 00:22:23.750
"Episode 9: 'Love That Embraces
the Holy Mother: Marigold'"

00:22:23.750 --> 00:22:27.000
"Episode 9: 'Love That Embraces
the Holy Mother: Marigold'"

00:22:23.750 --> 00:22:27.000
This is what I wanted.

00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:27.950
"Episode 9: 'Love That Embraces
the Holy Mother: Marigold'"

00:23:57.910 --> 00:23:58.750
"Next Time: 'Cherry Blossoms and
Spring and Spring and the Moon'"

00:23:58.750 --> 00:24:00.790
"Next Time: 'Cherry Blossoms and
Spring and Spring and the Moon'"

00:23:58.750 --> 00:24:00.790
Adashimapedia: Valentine's Day.

00:24:00.790 --> 00:24:03.290
"Next Time: 'Cherry Blossoms and
Spring and Spring and the Moon'"

00:24:00.790 --> 00:24:03.290
Nagafuji's Butcher Shop is doing
a Valentine's Day promotion, too!

00:24:03.290 --> 00:24:04.830
You selling chocolate-filled croquettes?

00:24:04.830 --> 00:24:06.500
Nothing that cliché.

00:24:06.500 --> 00:24:09.120
Grab your boy's heart with
a special on actual hearts!

00:24:09.120 --> 00:24:11.290
How would you feel getting offal from a girl?

00:24:11.290 --> 00:24:12.910
Let's fire up that grill!
